{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-880e1b6382a127ac","type":"tool_result","content":"# Qwen3-TTS Technical Report\narXiv: 2601.15621\nAuthors: Hangrui Hu, Xinfa Zhu, Ting He, Dake Guo, Bin Zhang, Xiong Wang, Zhifang Guo, Ziyue Jiang, Hongkun Hao, Zishan Guo, Xinyu Zhang, Pei Zhang, Baosong Yang, Jin Xu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of the Qwen3-TTS series, a family of advanced multilingual, controllable, robust, and streaming text-to-speech models.\n  2. Development of Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-25Hz, a single-codebook codec that integrates semantic and acoustic cues for seamless LLM integration and streaming waveform reconstruction.\n  3. Development of Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz, a multi-codebook codec achieving extreme bitrate reduction and ultra-low-latency streaming with a first-packet latency as low as 97 ms.\n  4. Design of a dual-track autoregressive language model architecture incorporating a Multi-Token Prediction module for real-time streaming synthesis.\n  5. Achievement of state-of-the-art performance in zero-shot voice cloning, cross-lingual speech generation, and natural language instruction-following for voice design.\n  6. Demonstration of exceptional stability in long-form generation, capable of synthesizing over 10 minutes of fluent speech without chunk-based artifacts.\n  7. Open-sourcing of the complete family of Qwen3-TTS models and tokenizers under the Apache 2.0 license to facilitate community research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/控制-NL描述, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"01e20723-82e6-4893-8019-155fae38aa81","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:17:37.506Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Qwen3-TTS Technical Report\narXiv: 2601.15621\nAuthors: Hangrui Hu, Xinfa Zhu, Ting He, Dake Guo, Bin Zhang, Xiong Wang, Zhifang Guo, Ziyue Jiang, Hongkun Hao, Zishan Guo, Xinyu Zhang, Pei Zhang, Baosong Yang, Jin Xu, Jingren Zhou, Junyang Lin\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of the Qwen3-TTS series, a family of advanced multilingual, controllable, robust, and streaming text-to-speech models.\n  2. Development of Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-25Hz, a single-codebook codec that integrates semantic and acoustic cues for seamless LLM integration and streaming waveform reconstruction.\n  3. Development of Qwen-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz, a multi-codebook codec achieving extreme bitrate reduction and ultra-low-latency streaming with a first-packet latency as low as 97 ms.\n  4. Design of a dual-track autoregressive language model architecture incorporating a Multi-Token Prediction module for real-time streaming synthesis.\n  5. Achievement of state-of-the-art performance in zero-shot voice cloning, cross-lingual speech generation, and natural language instruction-following for voice design.\n  6. Demonstration of exceptional stability in long-form generation, capable of synthesizing over 10 minutes of fluent speech without chunk-based artifacts.\n  7. Open-sourcing of the complete family of Qwen3-TTS models and tokenizers under the Apache 2.0 license to facilitate community research.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/控制-NL描述, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dfbd1384b572960","type":"tool_result","content":"# MiniMax-Speech: Intrinsic Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech with a Learnable Speaker Encoder\narXiv: 2505.07916\nAuthors: Bowen Zhang, Congchao Guo, Geng Yang, Hang Yu, Haozhe Zhang, Heidi Lei, Jialong Mai, Junjie Yan, Kaiyue Yang, Mingqi Yang, Peikai Huang, Ruiyang Jin, Sitan Jiang, Weihua Cheng, Yawei Li, Yichen Xiao, Yiying Zhou, Yongmao Zhang, Yuan Lu, Yucen He\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present MiniMax-Speech, a TTS model that supports 32 languages and generates high-fidelity speech, achieving SOTA results on multiple objective and subjective evaluation metrics.\n  2. Based on an autoregressive Transformer architecture equipped with a learnable speaker encoder, our model demonstrates strong expressiveness in zero-shot voice cloning and enhances speaker similarity in one-shot scenarios.\n  3. We employ a flow matching model based on our novel Flow-VAE, which further improves the audio quality and speaker similarity of the generated speech.\n  4. We detail several downstream applications of our model, including fine-grained control over emotional expression, extensive voice library via Text to Voice, and improving synthesis similarity by Professional Voice Clone.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"8fd9c644-8853-4a01-96cf-bf25695760d2","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:17:37.829Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# MiniMax-Speech: Intrinsic Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech with a Learnable Speaker Encoder\narXiv: 2505.07916\nAuthors: Bowen Zhang, Congchao Guo, Geng Yang, Hang Yu, Haozhe Zhang, Heidi Lei, Jialong Mai, Junjie Yan, Kaiyue Yang, Mingqi Yang, Peikai Huang, Ruiyang Jin, Sitan Jiang, Weihua Cheng, Yawei Li, Yichen Xiao, Yiying Zhou, Yongmao Zhang, Yuan Lu, Yucen He\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present MiniMax-Speech, a TTS model that supports 32 languages and generates high-fidelity speech, achieving SOTA results on multiple objective and subjective evaluation metrics.\n  2. Based on an autoregressive Transformer architecture equipped with a learnable speaker encoder, our model demonstrates strong expressiveness in zero-shot voice cloning and enhances speaker similarity in one-shot scenarios.\n  3. We employ a flow matching model based on our novel Flow-VAE, which further improves the audio quality and speaker similarity of the generated speech.\n  4. We detail several downstream applications of our model, including fine-grained control over emotional expression, extensive voice library via Text to Voice, and improving synthesis similarity by Professional Voice Clone.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a388b458c5200db6","type":"tool_result","content":"# \narXiv: 2605.05611\nAuthors: \nYear: 0 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present X-Voice, a highly efficient 0.4B flow-matching TTS system supporting 30 languages that achieves high-fidelity zero-shot voice cloning through tailored designs like Dual-level Language Injection and Decoupled Classifier-Free Guidance.\n  2. We fully open-source our 420K-hour training corpus, the 30K-hour high-quality subset, and a rigorously verified benchmark to establish an evaluation standard for zero-shot multilingual voice cloning.\n  3. We introduce a novel two-stage training pipeline that removes the model's dependence on reference transcripts during zero-shot voice cloning without relying on auxiliary modules or forced alignment.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"75f0321e-2ea4-4f8d-b9a9-458e2263c1ad","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:17:38.122Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# \narXiv: 2605.05611\nAuthors: \nYear: 0 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present X-Voice, a highly efficient 0.4B flow-matching TTS system supporting 30 languages that achieves high-fidelity zero-shot voice cloning through tailored designs like Dual-level Language Injection and Decoupled Classifier-Free Guidance.\n  2. We fully open-source our 420K-hour training corpus, the 30K-hour high-quality subset, and a rigorously verified benchmark to establish an evaluation standard for zero-shot multilingual voice cloning.\n  3. We introduce a novel two-stage training pipeline that removes the model's dependence on reference transcripts during zero-shot voice cloning without relying on auxiliary modules or forced alignment.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能