{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b989c3f93dd6a3b1","type":"tool_result","content":"# OmniVoice: Towards Omnilingual Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech with Diffusion Language Models\narXiv: 2604.00688\nAuthors: Han Zhu, Lingxuan Ye, Wei Kang, Zengwei Yao, Liyong Guo, Fangjun Kuang, Zhifeng Han, Weiji Zhuang, Long Lin, Daniel Povey\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a single-stage discrete non-autoregressive TTS architecture that directly maps text to multi-codebook acoustic tokens, bypassing the error propagation and information bottlenecks of two-stage pipelines.\n  2. Proposal of a full-codebook random masking strategy that enables dense loss computation across all codebooks to significantly enhance training efficiency and generative quality.\n  3. Demonstration that initializing the bidirectional Transformer backbone with pre-trained autoregressive LLM weights successfully resolves the intelligibility challenge in single-stage discrete NAR TTS models.\n  4. Creation of a 581k-hour multilingual dataset curated from open-source data, enabling the broadest language coverage to date for a zero-shot TTS model with support for over 600 languages.\n  5. Achievement of state-of-the-art performance in intelligibility, speaker similarity, and naturalness across Chinese, English, and diverse massive multilingual benchmarks.\n  6. Integration of multi-dimensional controllability features, including prompt denoising, speaker-attribute-based voice design, and fine-grained paralinguistic and phonetic control.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/功能-多语言","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"c7a0c90c-b5de-4df6-8e71-3d17b9ea2a00","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:21:08.895Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# OmniVoice: Towards Omnilingual Zero-Shot Text-to-Speech with Diffusion Language Models\narXiv: 2604.00688\nAuthors: Han Zhu, Lingxuan Ye, Wei Kang, Zengwei Yao, Liyong Guo, Fangjun Kuang, Zhifeng Han, Weiji Zhuang, Long Lin, Daniel Povey\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a single-stage discrete non-autoregressive TTS architecture that directly maps text to multi-codebook acoustic tokens, bypassing the error propagation and information bottlenecks of two-stage pipelines.\n  2. Proposal of a full-codebook random masking strategy that enables dense loss computation across all codebooks to significantly enhance training efficiency and generative quality.\n  3. Demonstration that initializing the bidirectional Transformer backbone with pre-trained autoregressive LLM weights successfully resolves the intelligibility challenge in single-stage discrete NAR TTS models.\n  4. Creation of a 581k-hour multilingual dataset curated from open-source data, enabling the broadest language coverage to date for a zero-shot TTS model with support for over 600 languages.\n  5. Achievement of state-of-the-art performance in intelligibility, speaker similarity, and naturalness across Chinese, English, and diverse massive multilingual benchmarks.\n  6. Integration of multi-dimensional controllability features, including prompt denoising, speaker-attribute-based voice design, and fine-grained paralinguistic and phonetic control.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/功能-多语言","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
