{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae07c38ddf629b4f","type":"tool_result","content":"# CosyVoice 3: Towards In-the-wild Speech Generation via Scaling-up and Post-training\narXiv: 2505.17589\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Changfeng Gao, Yuxuan Wang, Fan Yu, Tianyu Zhao, Hao Wang, Xiang Lv, Hui Wang, Chongjia Ni, Xian Shi, Keyu An, Guanrou Yang, Yabin Li, Yanni Chen, Zhifu Gao, Qian Chen, Yue Gu, Mengzhe Chen, Yafeng Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Wen Wang, Jieping Ye\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose a novel speech tokenizer derived from a large audio understanding model via supervised multi-task training to better capture paralinguistic information.\n  2. We introduce a differentiable reward optimization (DiffRO) method for post-training that directly optimizes speech tokens using back-propagation.\n  3. We validate dataset size scaling by expanding training data from ten thousand to one million hours, covering 9 languages and 18 Chinese dialects.\n  4. We demonstrate model size scaling by increasing parameters from 0.5 billion to 1.5 billion, which enhances prosody naturalness and performance on difficult tasks.\n  5. We release the CV3-Eval benchmark for zero-shot speech synthesis in the wild, featuring authentic in-the-wild data across diverse languages, domains, and emotions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-方言小语种, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-混合","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"870451ba-0d93-403b-b382-7a6147c9b93e","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:21:46.504Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# CosyVoice 3: Towards In-the-wild Speech Generation via Scaling-up and Post-training\narXiv: 2505.17589\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Changfeng Gao, Yuxuan Wang, Fan Yu, Tianyu Zhao, Hao Wang, Xiang Lv, Hui Wang, Chongjia Ni, Xian Shi, Keyu An, Guanrou Yang, Yabin Li, Yanni Chen, Zhifu Gao, Qian Chen, Yue Gu, Mengzhe Chen, Yafeng Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Wen Wang, Jieping Ye\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose a novel speech tokenizer derived from a large audio understanding model via supervised multi-task training to better capture paralinguistic information.\n  2. We introduce a differentiable reward optimization (DiffRO) method for post-training that directly optimizes speech tokens using back-propagation.\n  3. We validate dataset size scaling by expanding training data from ten thousand to one million hours, covering 9 languages and 18 Chinese dialects.\n  4. We demonstrate model size scaling by increasing parameters from 0.5 billion to 1.5 billion, which enhances prosody naturalness and performance on difficult tasks.\n  5. We release the CV3-Eval benchmark for zero-shot speech synthesis in the wild, featuring authentic in-the-wild data across diverse languages, domains, and emotions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-方言小语种, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-混合","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abd8021bf1c71b2b","type":"tool_result","content":"# Cross-Lingual F5-TTS: Towards Language-Agnostic Voice Cloning and Speech Synthesis\narXiv: 2509.14579\nAuthors: Qingyu Liu, Yushen Chen, Zhikang Niu, Chunhui Wang, Yunting Yang, Bowen Zhang, Jian Zhao, Pengcheng Zhu, Kai Yu, Xie Chen\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of Cross-Lingual F5-TTS, a framework that enables cross-lingual zero-shot voice cloning without requiring audio prompt transcripts.\n  2. Utilization of MMS forced alignment to extract word boundaries for preprocessing training data, allowing direct synthesis from audio prompts while excluding transcripts.\n  3. Development of dedicated speaking rate predictors at phoneme, syllable, and word granularities to estimate target speech duration directly from acoustic features.\n  4. Formulation of speaking rate prediction as a discrete classification task trained with a Gaussian Cross-Entropy loss to account for the ordinal nature of speaking rate categories.\n  5. Demonstration that the proposed transcript-free approach achieves comparable performance to the F5-TTS baseline in intra-lingual scenarios while successfully enabling cross-lingual voice cloning for unseen languages.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"24cb4e3b-3f9b-4bd0-9816-019f147c8435","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:21:46.787Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Cross-Lingual F5-TTS: Towards Language-Agnostic Voice Cloning and Speech Synthesis\narXiv: 2509.14579\nAuthors: Qingyu Liu, Yushen Chen, Zhikang Niu, Chunhui Wang, Yunting Yang, Bowen Zhang, Jian Zhao, Pengcheng Zhu, Kai Yu, Xie Chen\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of Cross-Lingual F5-TTS, a framework that enables cross-lingual zero-shot voice cloning without requiring audio prompt transcripts.\n  2. Utilization of MMS forced alignment to extract word boundaries for preprocessing training data, allowing direct synthesis from audio prompts while excluding transcripts.\n  3. Development of dedicated speaking rate predictors at phoneme, syllable, and word granularities to estimate target speech duration directly from acoustic features.\n  4. Formulation of speaking rate prediction as a discrete classification task trained with a Gaussian Cross-Entropy loss to account for the ordinal nature of speaking rate categories.\n  5. Demonstration that the proposed transcript-free approach achieves comparable performance to the F5-TTS baseline in intra-lingual scenarios while successfully enabling cross-lingual voice cloning for unseen languages.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
