{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-920ffc9d5c384c7b","type":"tool_result","content":"# CosyVoice 2: Scalable Streaming Speech Synthesis with Large Language Models\narXiv: 2412.10117\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Yuxuan Wang, Qian Chen, Xian Shi, Xiang Lv, Tianyu Zhao, Zhifu Gao, Yexin Yang, Changfeng Gao, Hui Wang, Fan Yu, Huadai Liu, Zhengyan Sheng, Yue Gu, Chong Deng, Wen Wang, Shiliang Zhang, Zhijie Yan, Jingren Zhou\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introducing CosyVoice 2, a scalable streaming speech synthesis model that integrates large language models with a speech decoder.\n  2. Designing a unified architecture that seamlessly supports both streaming and non-streaming speech synthesis.\n  3. Developing a large language model equipped with block-wise causal attention to effectively balance lookahead context and streaming latency.\n  4. Implementing a modified finite scalar quantization strategy with an adaptive weight to achieve high-compression and high-accuracy speech tokenization.\n  5. Demonstrating through comprehensive experiments that the proposed model significantly outperforms its predecessor and achieves state-of-the-art performance in speech synthesis.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/控制-参考语音","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"3aca03cf-9985-42b2-9f16-1ffe8b4b544a","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:22:22.111Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# CosyVoice 2: Scalable Streaming Speech Synthesis with Large Language Models\narXiv: 2412.10117\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Yuxuan Wang, Qian Chen, Xian Shi, Xiang Lv, Tianyu Zhao, Zhifu Gao, Yexin Yang, Changfeng Gao, Hui Wang, Fan Yu, Huadai Liu, Zhengyan Sheng, Yue Gu, Chong Deng, Wen Wang, Shiliang Zhang, Zhijie Yan, Jingren Zhou\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introducing CosyVoice 2, a scalable streaming speech synthesis model that integrates large language models with a speech decoder.\n  2. Designing a unified architecture that seamlessly supports both streaming and non-streaming speech synthesis.\n  3. Developing a large language model equipped with block-wise causal attention to effectively balance lookahead context and streaming latency.\n  4. Implementing a modified finite scalar quantization strategy with an adaptive weight to achieve high-compression and high-accuracy speech tokenization.\n  5. Demonstrating through comprehensive experiments that the proposed model significantly outperforms its predecessor and achieves state-of-the-art performance in speech synthesis.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/控制-参考语音","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a87ae3eadfd432ff","type":"tool_result","content":"# MOSS-TTS Technical Report\narXiv: 2603.18090\nAuthors: Yitian Gong, Botian Jiang, Yiwei Zhao, Yucheng Yuan, Kuangwei Chen, Yaozhou Jiang, Cheng Chang, Dong Hong, Mingshu Chen, Ruixiao Li, Yiyang Zhang, Yang Gao, Hanfu Chen, Ke Chen, Songlin Wang, Xiaogui Yang, Yuqian Zhang, Kexin Huang, ZhengYuan Lin, Kang Yu, Ziqi Chen, Jin Wang, Zhaoye Fei, Qinyuan Cheng, Shimin Li, Xipeng Qiu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Development of MOSS-Audio-Tokenizer, a causal Transformer tokenizer that compresses 24 kHz audio to 12.5 fps using variable-bitrate RVQ and unified semantic-acoustic representations.\n  2. Release of MOSS-TTS, an autoregressive generator emphasizing structural simplicity, scalability, and long-context or control-oriented deployment.\n  3. Introduction of MOSS-TTS-Local-Transformer, which incorporates a frame-local autoregressive module for higher modeling efficiency, stronger speaker preservation, and reduced time to first audio.\n  4. Demonstration of comprehensive generation capabilities including zero-shot voice cloning, token-level duration control, phoneme- and pinyin-level pronunciation control, smooth code-switching, and stable long-form generation.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/量化-RVQ","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f6e3cba-af47-4a0f-b763-e6b948eddb30","uuid":"58405c0d-fa51-44b9-bc0c-2349334a2b54","timestamp":"2026-08-13T07:22:22.396Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# MOSS-TTS Technical Report\narXiv: 2603.18090\nAuthors: Yitian Gong, Botian Jiang, Yiwei Zhao, Yucheng Yuan, Kuangwei Chen, Yaozhou Jiang, Cheng Chang, Dong Hong, Mingshu Chen, Ruixiao Li, Yiyang Zhang, Yang Gao, Hanfu Chen, Ke Chen, Songlin Wang, Xiaogui Yang, Yuqian Zhang, Kexin Huang, ZhengYuan Lin, Kang Yu, Ziqi Chen, Jin Wang, Zhaoye Fei, Qinyuan Cheng, Shimin Li